  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) An AC generator works on the electromagnetic induction principle. So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>(B)&nbsp;The transformer works on the principle of mutual induction.&nbsp;So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p>(C)&nbsp;Resonance occurs when the value of inductive and capacitive reactance have equal magnitude but a phase difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.&nbsp; So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>(D) The sharpness of resonance is defined using the quality&nbsp;factor which explains how fast energy decay in an oscillating system.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>D</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;</p>"
